    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2405" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱμᾰσιά</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wall</i> of dry stones, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱμασιάς τε λέγειν</span> to lay
			<i>walls</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.359
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ. λέξοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					24.224
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.69
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				7.22
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ. ἐγγεγλυμμένη τύποισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.138
				</span></i>
			: of the walls of a city or fortress, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1.180
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				191
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.43
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ. περιοικοδομῆσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					55.11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφ᾽ αἱμασιῇσιν ἥμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					1.47
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(3).248
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Anaphe</span>).</div>
